      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Overall I find there's just often inconsistencies with how hands are handled relative to controllers in VRChat. I play on a HP Reverb G2, and by default all hands are offset a fair bit to the front, and depending on avatar the angles can be off too. I think the best solution here would be some kind of offset options.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "62e5a9448bdeb344c10d287b",
      "author": {
        "_id": "5f2d2f4df6abbf61555a67b7",
        "alias": "Educational Grouse",
        "aliasID": "65c35355ed6eefce4cb89a0b",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny-assets.io/images/013fd4676b522cf00c9d76fcd62696c3.png",
        "created": "2020-08-07T10:39:09.328Z",
        "name": "Alex the Cat",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": "alex-the-cat"
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "621946996d11764c11ffcf01",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2022-07-30T21:57:24.968Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "6292394a39266e0b710ed446",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 2
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "My avatar's hands are rotated about 50 degrees back from my irl hands. Its very uncanny and upsetting. It happens on every avatar. I believe it might have something to do with different size hands having to grip the index controller differently - my friends' avatar hands are also rotated incorrectly, but to a lesser degree more like the image OP posted. The IK assumes that one would grip the controller at a perfect 90 degree angle to the controller, which i dont think is feasable for anyone to do. My hands are more off than others angle wise because I have small hands and have a permanently injured thumb, forcing me to grip the index further up to reach the joystick. \nHaving a way to change hand rotation and offset would help everyone, both people like me with a very large difference in angle due to disability and also just normal people who want to have hands that match their own properly.\nRight now the difference between irl hands and in-game hands makes me feel a bit sick the whole time I'm in vrchat.\nI would be very happy to have any method of adjusting this, even if its in a launch option or config doc.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "62ea500358f49666dfb10613",
      "author": {
        "_id": "6224599590c90b51a1096996",
        "alias": "Green Squid",
        "aliasID": "65c3e658ed6eefce4cb8a90d",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": null,
        "created": "2022-03-06T06:49:57.260Z",
        "name": "Itsuki1",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": "itsuki1"
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "621946996d11764c11ffcf01",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2022-08-03T10:37:55.267Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": "62ec726738e71d263de34d63",
      "mergedPostDetails": "Hey there, index controllers have a huge problem of the hand angles being off by 10-15 degrees, every single friend of mine that uses index (and if any of them are reading this please comment) has the same problem.\nAs we all know not all avatars are the same and it would be great to have an option to manually shift the hand angles, as we all know hands in vr are what we use to interact with everything and seeing them not allign with real life ones is simply immersion breaking (and a lot of people will agree with me on this one)\nThe solution would be instead of changing it for everyone let everyone change it for themselves, either on runtime or in launch options as same as other launch options for ik-2, example \"-Hand-y-offset x\" where \"x\" is the number. Same for x and z axis. \nHere are some pictures showing the problem, the problem persists on every single avatar, doesn't matter if it's 3, 6 and 11 point tracking.\nAnd as said, having an option to change the hands offset manually would greatly improve the experience.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Valve index controllers bad angles.",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "6292394a39266e0b710ed446",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 1
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Yeah i have seen many other users and my friends  have this problem as well. Most have said it is very immersion breaking and wise there was a way to fix this problem i think a fix would be very appreciated",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
