      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{6161a61a2c0de966b4e43486|full_name}: Hey Kung, thank you for your work and for this welcome feature! Really appreciate your work.\nI need to ask you about something because you merged my old post as well as ALEKSIS-SENPAI's posts in here but we were asking about something different.\nI saw the example video in the Dev Update and it looks great, but we don't really depend on the angle of the controller, we need to be able to offset by the Y and Z axes at the very least too.\nOur hands just touch the the bottom of our controllers and are too far back on the Z axis, just that wrist rotation doesn't fix it.\nAt this point I've taken to just offsetting my hand bones in Blender, which is really janky and breaks the weights of animations slightly but it's still not as bad as having the hand 5cm too low.\nI’ve asked all my friends if theirs are off too, and they all are off on the Y axis by at least a couple centimeters, some more and some less.\nI really am begging you please give us sliders for these axes, please. :( I very much depend on it and it affects almost everybody.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
