      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{6227bbaf8e19345f3a86a491|full_name}: I merged your previous post because it was mainly focused on your hand being \"off\" and listed both position and angle. And this Canny broadly seeks to resolve the hand being \"off\" without unneeded menu bloat (for example you could have 6 total sliders per hand for a total of 12 for absolute full control, but that's gonna bloat the menu too much even for advanced options). I'm about to mark this Canny as complete so if it's not too much trouble could you make another Canny post specifically detailing why you need positional offset as well, and specifically what axis of offset you need? If you can demonstrate that on avatars that don't have an offset wrist bone workaround that would be best.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
